DevOps lifecycle: Plan → Code → Build → Test → Release → Deploy → Operate → Monitor in english
Here’s the DevOps lifecycle explained in simple English:

🔄 DevOps Lifecycle Stages
Plan → Decide what to build, set goals, and create tasks.

Code → Write the application code.

Build → Compile code, create packages or Docker images.

Test → Run automated/manual tests to check quality.

Release → Prepare the software for deployment.

Deploy → Move the software into production (live environment).

Operate → Run and manage the application in production.

Monitor → Track performance, errors, and user feedback.

